Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:49:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(chat): store uploaded images in the workspace's
 object storage

In workspace mode, JPG / PNG / WebP attachments are uploaded through the
workspace (/api/uploads, the same bucket as video and image references)
and the chat history keeps only the image URL instead of the whole
base64 image, so the history on the server stays small. Before a request
goes to the model, the browser fetches those images again and inlines
them as data URLs; an image that has expired is replaced by a short note
instead of failing the request. Other image types are still inlined as
before. Opening /chat directly also opens the media session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
